From: Yongzhao Chen <yongzhao.derek@gmail.com>
Subject: wifi: ath11k: read the HTT completion status at the right offset

ath11k_dp_tx_completion_valid() (244) finds the HTT status of a
firmware-released tx completion with

  ((struct htt_tx_wbm_completion *)desc) + HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_STATUS_OFFSET

HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_STATUS_OFFSET is a byte offset (8), but the cast makes
it count 16-byte structs, so the filter reads desc + 128: the buffer
address of the release entry four slots further on. Whenever bits 12:9
of that unrelated address happen to be 5, the completion is taken for
HAL_WBM_REL_HTT_TX_COMP_STATUS_MEC_NOTIFY and skipped. Its skb then
stays in the tx idr pool, DMA mapped, and num_tx_pending never comes
down; nothing is logged.

The firmware releases mostly multicast and broadcast frames, so those
are the ones lost. On a Redmi AX5400 (IPQ5018 + QCN9074, NSS offload
off) num_tx_pending reached 1384 on 5 GHz and 322 on 2.4 GHz within
days and the router ran out of memory. With this change it stays at
0-4 over 24 hours and no completion is skipped.

Use byte arithmetic, as ath11k_dp_tx_process_htt_tx_complete() does.

Signed-off-by: Yongzhao Chen <yongzhao.derek@gmail.com>
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -804,7 +804,7 @@ static inline bool ath11k_dp_tx_completi
 
 	if (FIELD_GET(HAL_WBM_RELEASE_INFO0_REL_SRC_MODULE, desc->info0) ==
 	    HAL_WBM_REL_SRC_MODULE_FW) {
-		status_desc = ((struct htt_tx_wbm_completion *)desc) + HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_STATUS_OFFSET;
+		status_desc = (void *)desc + HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_STATUS_OFFSET;
 
 		/* Dont consider HTT_TX_COMP_STATUS_MEC_NOTIFY */
 		if (FIELD_GET(HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_INFO0_STATUS, status_desc->info0) ==
